-- title:
--   Generic fibre of the full-level moduli ring: reduced, of rank ψ(M')|GL₂(𝔽_ℓ)||GL₂(𝔽_q)|/2
-- statement:
--   Fix primes $q\ge 5$ and $\ell\ge 3$ with $\ell\ne q$, and a nonzero natural number $M'$ divisible by neither $q$ nor $\ell$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero containing a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity $\xi$ for which some ring homomorphism $L\to\mathbb{C}$ sends $\xi$ to $e^{2\pi i/(q\ell)}$, and let $K$ be the intermediate field of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of $X_H$ of level $(q\ell)^2M'$, where $H=\mathtt{levelH}\,(q\ell)\,M'$ is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/(q\ell)^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$ whose maximal ideal contains $q$, acting on $K$ compatibly, and let $j\in K$, nonzero, have image the $j$-series [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157). Assume $\ell$ and $M'$ are units in $A$; assume the two equivariance hypotheses that level-$\ell$ data (`LevelPData` satisfying `IsLevelPStructure`) and $\Gamma_0(p^k)$-kernel polynomials (`IsGamma0PowAt`) transport along Weierstrass variable changes; let $\mathcal{G}$ be a family of relative group laws on the projective models that is chord–tangent and has the origin as identity, and $\mathcal{T}$ a level transport for Drinfeld bases of level $q$ satisfying `IsSectionTransport`; assume further that every variable change and every coefficient change of an $A$-algebra is realised by a graded ring homomorphism of projective-model rings with the stated irrelevant-ideal condition. Let $P_0$ be a fine moduli package for the rigid datum `rigidDataPow A ℓ M' q …`, that is, an $A$-algebra $B_0$ of finite type with a universal point such that points of the datum over any $A$-algebra $T$ correspond bijectively to $A$-algebra maps $B_0\to T$; suppose a point $x$ of the datum over $K$ has $j$-invariant the series [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18). Writing $S$ for the $A$-subalgebra of $B_0$ generated by the distinguished element `P₀.j₀` and assuming $S$ a domain with fraction field $F$, the conclusion is that $F\otimes_S B_0$ is reduced and $$\dim_F\bigl(F\otimes_S B_0\bigr)=\Bigl(\prod_{p\mid M'}p^{v_p(M')-1}(p+1)\Bigr)\cdot\#GL_2(\mathbb{Z}/\ell)\cdot\#GL_2(\mathbb{Z}/q)\,/\,2,$$ the division being in $\mathbb{N}$.
--
--   This identifies the generic fibre of the fine moduli ring of the combined moduli problem ($\Gamma_0$-structure of level $M'$, level-$\ell$ structure, Drinfeld basis of level $q$) over the $j$-line: it is reduced, and its degree over the $j$-line is $\psi(M')\,\#GL_2(\mathbb{F}_\ell)\,\#GL_2(\mathbb{F}_q)/2$. It feeds the counting of minimal primes of $B_0$ and the subsequent identification of the irreducible components of the full-level modular curve with the analytically defined ones.
-- source:
